只输出严格JSON，恰好包含id（metadata.id原样）、summary_zh（15到140个Unicode字符，通常40到100字）、category（枚举）、tags（2到5个不重复关键词，每个最多30字符）、confidence（0到1，仅自评）、insufficient_evidence（布尔）、evidence（1到3个对象，每个恰好包含paragraph_id、fact）、limitations（0到5个字符串）。只选择输入中长度20至120字符的完整片段编号；fact是该片段支持的中文事实转述。不要输出quote，不要自行抄写、拼接、删改或补造引用。程序会按编号附上原文。一个编号只用一次；最多3条证据。不得增加字段。
摘要和limitations保留会改变功能意义的前提、平台例外和限制：设密码后才认证、页面保持打开才提醒、依赖外部组件、估算不等于保证。只写已实现功能，不将规划当完成。证据不足就标记，不编造。
图像识别/分类不是媒体创作，没有贴切类别归other；量化、计算与领域研究归search-research，不因多智能体实现归agents-automation；模型/CLI适配与插件开发工具归coding-development；市场/精选目录按搜索发现归search-research。不要按附属同步、备份或评论功能分类。不要推断本机客户端等于本地模型。
摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Terminal-native frontend for DeepSeek Harness with real scrollback; a direct, in-process consumer of Harness capabilities.","id":"gh:1337055793","install_available":false,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dshline","slug":"riesbri/dshline","topics":["ai-agent","cli","cordis","deepseek","deepseek-harness","developer-tools","dsh-plugin","nodejs","terminal","tui","typescript"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Terminal-native frontend for DeepSeek Harness with real scrollback; a direct, in-process consumer of"},{"id":"p1s2","text":" Harness capabilities."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dshline"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"English | 中文"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"**A terminal-native frontend for DeepSeek Harness.**"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"An agent in your terminal — not instead of it. Finished output stays in your terminal's own scrollba"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"ck; only a bounded live region redraws."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"dshline runs in-process as a direct consumer of Harness capabilities rather than creating a parallel"},{"id":"p6s2","text":" agent runtime or state layer."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"**Website:** dshline.xyz"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"## See it in action"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"The first run asks once before letting Harness create the `dshline` profile and install this package"},{"id":"p11s2","text":" into it. It needs `pnpm` on your `PATH`, because the harness installs profile plugins with pnpm; it"},{"id":"p11s3","text":" checks before it changes anything and says so if it is missing. See Install for requirements, verif"},{"id":"p11s4","text":"ication, explicit setup with `dshline --setup`, and source installs."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"**Harness compatibility:** dshline supports one Harness generation at a time. If npm reports a depen"},{"id":"p12s2","text":"dency conflict or `/setup` reports a Harness version mismatch, do not use `--force` or `--legacy-pee"},{"id":"p12s3","text":"r-deps`; see Installation → Harness version mismatch."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"> [!WARNING]\n> Sandbox and tool permissions are controlled by the active Harness profile; ordinary t"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"ool calls may run without per-call review. See Permissions and the sandbox before using dshline on i"},{"id":"p13s3","text":"run without per-call review. See Permissions and the sandbox before using dshline on important code."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"## Why dshline?"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"Harness plugins publish capabilities; dshline presents supported capabilities natively in the termin"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"al. It consumes Harness contracts rather than creating separate provider runtimes, state stores, or "},{"id":"p15s3","text":"consumes Harness contracts rather than creating separate provider runtimes, state stores, or policy."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"`Harness plugin → standard capability → dshline presentation adapter → native terminal UI`"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"Harness owns capabilities, state, runtime, persistence, and policy. dshline owns terminal presentati"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"ness owns capabilities, state, runtime, persistence, and policy. dshline owns terminal presentation."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"### Generic capability integration"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"dshline integrates through standard Harness capabilities instead of provider-specific code. Work con"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"sumes `ctx.jobs` and `ctx.subagents`; Sessions uses `ctx.sessionQuery`; `/connect` uses Harness's mo"},{"id":"p19s3","text":"del, settings, credentials, and authorization services; `/plugins` reads and switches the running ag"},{"id":"p19s4","text":"ent's composition through `ctx.agentPresets`; `/profiles` reads the profile roster through Harness's"},{"id":"p19s5","text":" own home-path service and forwards every change to `dsh plugin`. New providers can therefore flow t"},{"id":"p19s6","text":"hrough existing interfaces without requiring a dedicated dshline implementation. A real Codex provid"},{"id":"p19s7","text":"er has already passed this boundary through generic `ctx.subagents` and `ctx.jobs` presentation, wit"},{"id":"p19s8","text":"h no provider-specific dshline production code; see Provider acceptance."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"It ships no provider list and no login protocol: `/connect` offers whatever the mounted adapters dec"},{"id":"p20s2","text":"lare configurable and runs whatever flows Harness has registered, so the same providers are reachabl"},{"id":"p20s3","text":"e from the terminal and from the official web Models page, over one settings document and one creden"},{"id":"p20s4","text":"terminal and from the official web Models page, over one settings document and one credential store."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"See Architecture for the capability model and current adapter boundaries."},{"id":"p22s1","text":"### Native terminal by design"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"Finished output is committed to real terminal scrollback and never rewritten. Normal scrolling, sele"},{"id":"p23s2","text":"ction, and copying keep working while dshline redraws only a bounded live region. The Harness-indepe"},{"id":"p23s3","text":"ndent renderer stays small, dependency-light, and focused on terminal correctness: widths, Unicode, "},{"id":"p23s4","text":"escaping, keys, and safe redraws."},{"id":"p24s1","text":"See Design for the terminal invariants and Comparison for the trade-offs."},{"id":"p25s1","text":"## Use dshline"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"Type `/` to discover the commands and capabilities available in the active Harness profile."},{"id":"p27s1","text":"- `/new` — start a fresh session in the current workspace; the previous one is reopenable when the a"},{"id":"p27s2","text":"ctive Harness profile provides session persistence\n- `/clear` — wipe the screen and start a fresh se"},{"id":"p27s3","text":"ssion in the current workspace, like `/new`; the previous one is reopenable when the active Harness "},{"id":"p27s4","text":"profile provides session persistence\n- `/image <path>` — stage a PNG, JPEG, WebP, or GIF as a real H"},{"id":"p27s5","text":"arness image for the next prompt; `@path` remains a textual reference\n- `/attach <path>` — attach an"},{"id":"p27s6","text":"y file verbatim for the next prompt, as a real Harness file; `@path` remains a textual reference and"},{"id":"p27s7","text":" `/image` remains the image gesture\n- `/sessions` — browse and resume Harness sessions\n- `/worktrees"},{"id":"p27s8","text":"` — choose a working directory represented in your Harness session history, then a conversation ther"},{"id":"p27s9","text":"e or a new one\n- `/work` — inspect workflows, subagents, and jobs\n- `/subagents` — browse this sessi"},{"id":"p27s10","text":"on's durable subagent conversations, inspect one, and continue a continuable child; also reachable w"},{"id":"p27s11","text":"ith `c` from `/work`\n- `/connect` — configure providers through Harness\n- `/plugins` — browse, searc"},{"id":"p27s12","text":"h, and customize the running agent's Harness preset composition\n- `/profiles` — browse Harness profi"},{"id":"p27s13","text":"les and the bundles each one composes; install, update, or remove one\n- `/todos` — inspect projected"},{"id":"p27s14","text":" Todo state\n- `/model` — switch registered models\n- `/theme` — choose the colour palette this window"},{"id":"p27s15","text":"\n- `/model` — switch registered models\n- `/theme` — choose the colour palette this window draws with"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"Usage covers keys, sessions, commands, and permission guidance."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"## Contributing"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"Contributions are welcome, especially generic capability adapters, terminal robustness, cross-platfo"},{"id":"p30s2","text":"rm verification, Unicode/CJK correctness, sessions, attachments, and focused UX improvements. Start "},{"id":"p30s3","text":"with CONTRIBUTING.md, then read AGENTS.md and the canonical Roadmap."},{"id":"p31s1","text":"## Documentation"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"- Install\n- Usage\n- Architecture\n- Design\n- Roadmap\n- Comparison\n- Contributing\n- Security"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"## License"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"MIT. Not affiliated with or endorsed by DeepSeek."}],"truncated":false}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
